# Fail fast on incompatible dependency bumps.
#
# By default npm silently overrides conflicting peer ranges and only emits a
# warning. That lets a bad toolchain bump install cleanly and then blow up
# much later at lint time with an error that points at the wrong thing —
# e.g. typescript@7 installs over typescript-eslint's ">=4.8.4 <6.1.0" peer,
# then typescript-eslint throws "does not support TS 7.0" at module load.
#
# With strict mode, those bumps fail here at install time and name the package
# that actually blocks them, so CI reports the real cause instead of a
# TypeError from inside a lint rule.
#
# Current pins in package.json are compatible with strict mode.
# Escape hatch for a one-off local install:  npm install --no-strict-peer-deps
strict-peer-deps=true